WEBVTT

00:00:01.062 --> 00:00:08.870
Welcome to vNAAATS. In this video, you will learn how VACS and TrackAudio work with the flight data display in FDD for Windows.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:17.030
Please note this is a demonstration using sample flights. It is not a live version of the FDD.

00:00:20.454 --> 00:00:27.846
FDD for Windows looks after your other programs. When you choose your position, it can open EuroScope, Vaxx, and your audio client for you.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.686
You choose which ones in the app setup screen under settings, app setup.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:36.838
For this video we will use VACS for controller calls and TrackAudio for voice with pilots.

00:00:37.542 --> 00:00:53.440
First a quick explanation. VACS is a free voice system for VATSIM controllers. It lets you make calls to other controllers, a bit like the telephone lines between air traffic units in real life. TrackAudio is a free audio client for VATSIM controllers and an alternative to audio for VATSIM.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:01:04.230
It is what you use to hear and talk to pilots on your frequencies. Now let us set up VACs so the FDD can see your calls. This uses a VAC setting called Remote Control, which is off by default.

00:01:04.486 --> 00:01:07.078
you need VACS version 2.1.0 or newer.

00:01:07.302 --> 00:01:19.238
In VACS, open Advanced Settings and tick Enable Remote Control. Then set the Listen Address to 127.0.0.1 colon 9600 so that only your own computer can connect.

00:01:19.622 --> 00:01:29.094
In FDD for Windows, the VACS call alert is already switched on, so once VACS is running, the headphones button at the top of the display connects by itself and shows VACS.

00:01:29.318 --> 00:01:36.390
If it says "VACS offline," check that VACS is running, that remote control is ticked, and that the port is 9,600.

00:01:37.158 --> 00:01:43.462
When someone calls you the headphones button flashes red with the caller's name and a pop-up appears, press accept to answer.

00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:51.270
Dismiss only hides the pop-up and the call keeps ringing in VACS. While you are on a call, the button shows in call and the name of the other controller.

00:01:52.102 --> 00:02:04.038
TrackAudio is the audio client for voice with pilots. The FDD can show you who spoke last on your frequencies. It talks to TrackAudio on your own computer only. No audio is recorded and nothing is sent to our server.

00:02:04.454 --> 00:02:08.166
the audio button and switch it on. Track audio needs to be running.

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.982
The button now shows who is talking right now.

00:02:11.206 --> 00:02:23.590
When they stop, it shows who spoke last and how long ago. Click it for the list of recent calls with the call sign frequency, time and length. They are kept on your computer for 24 hours. Click a call sign to select that aircraft.

00:02:24.358 --> 00:02:33.606
The aircraft that is transmitting gets a green box around its row in the flight list. The box fades out when it stops talking. If the row is off screen, the list scrolls to it.

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:37.414
Both can be switched off with the tick boxes in the TrackAudio window.

00:02:38.854 --> 00:02:41.990
To use TrackAudio on a second screen, press pop out.

00:02:42.278 --> 00:02:46.694
The history opens in its own window and keeps working while you use the main display.

00:02:47.558 --> 00:02:55.974
That is VACS and TrackAudio in the FDD. For the other how-to videos and the oceanic training notes, visit vnayats.com/training.

00:02:56.198 --> 00:02:57.570
Thanks for watching.

